B.am_=new A.cj("Some pictures aren't made by AI from scratch: a real photo has one part changed with an AI tool, like added fire, new handwriting or a different sky. The general check looks at the whole picture, so a small edit can slip past it.\n\nThe piece-by-piece check looks at the picture in 16 overlapping pieces, one at a time, and marks in red the ones that look AI-made on their own. It takes longer.\n\nA piece is judged without the rest of the picture, so it's less reliable than the general check: parts of real photos can light up too. Use it to see where to look, not as proof.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
